180
00:10:19,612 --> 00:10:22,213
The assignment has three questions. One:

181
00:10:22,233 --> 00:10:26,800
Vendor A's inspector has 90 percent recall and 5 percent false alarms,

182
00:10:26,820 --> 00:10:31,779
and the defect rate is 3 percent. Find alarms per 1000 pieces and precision.

183
00:10:31,799 --> 00:10:36,825
With a miss costing 30 yuan and a false alarm 1 yuan, find the cost per 1000;

184
00:10:36,845 --> 00:10:41,608
if a higher threshold gives 80 percent recall and 2 percent false alarms,

185
00:10:41,628 --> 00:10:45,671
what's the cost then? Which threshold would you pick, and why?

186
00:10:46,071 --> 00:10:51,044
Two: Vendor B claims a d-prime of 3.53. Using the equal-variance normal model,

187
00:10:51,064 --> 00:10:54,950
with 2 percent defects, 20 yuan per miss and 0.5 per recheck,

188
00:10:54,970 --> 00:10:58,151
find the cheapest threshold and the cost per 1000.

189
00:10:58,171 --> 00:11:02,824
If the section needs at least 80 percent precision and 90 percent recall,

190
00:11:02,844 --> 00:11:05,513
can B deliver, and what d-prime is needed?

191
00:11:05,913 --> 00:11:08,522
Three: write an acceptance and operating plan.

192
00:11:08,542 --> 00:11:12,922
Which metrics will you validate on your own section's samples before go-live,

193
00:11:12,942 --> 00:11:16,236
how will you re-validate when the style or fabric changes,

194
00:11:16,256 --> 00:11:20,750
how are false alarms and misses collected and how often is the model retrained,

195
00:11:20,770 --> 00:11:23,436
and who adjusts the threshold, using what data?

196
