204
00:11:54,685 --> 00:11:57,361
Three things to remember from the last lecture.

205
00:11:57,761 --> 00:12:00,850
One: of any AI application ask what data it eats,

206
00:12:00,870 --> 00:12:03,071
how it's judged and where it fails;

207
00:12:03,091 --> 00:12:05,862
each of the four kinds has its own weakness.

208
00:12:06,262 --> 00:12:09,559
Two: recall and false-alarm rate belong to the inspector,

209
00:12:09,579 --> 00:12:12,351
while precision also depends on the defect rate;

210
00:12:12,371 --> 00:12:15,552
set thresholds by the costs of misses and false alarms,

211
00:12:15,572 --> 00:12:19,683
and to have both high precision and high recall you must raise d-prime;

212
00:12:19,703 --> 00:12:24,105
judge predictive maintenance on lead time, false alarms and misses together.

213
00:12:24,505 --> 00:12:27,956
Three: an AI sewing machine is mostly sensors, actuators and control,

214
00:12:27,976 --> 00:12:30,069
so adjustments need limits and protection,

215
00:12:30,089 --> 00:12:33,842
and language assistants must cite sources and wait for a person to confirm.

216
